        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"strindberg-froken-julie-f75e1e15f1a3e50c\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.96,\"analysis\":\"Jean directly avows love and reinforces the assertion with “without doubt—can you doubt it?” The utterance does not itself undertake a commitment, and its hesitant, responsive, controlled delivery supplies no independent evidence of expressive/reflexive discharge.\",\"ambiguity\":\"Jean’s sincerity and possible strategic motives remain uncertain, but those issues do not alter the utterance’s strongly truth-conditional mode. The surrounding escape plan creates relational implications without making this sentence an undertaking.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Jean directly addresses Miss Julie in dramatic dialogue, saying “Jag älskar er” after she asks him to say that he loves her.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Miss Julie solicits the declaration as reassurance and courage for their proposed flight. Jean answers affirmatively but hesitates, declines immediate physical intimacy, retains the formal pronoun “er,” and stresses the barriers imposed by the house and the Count. His later promise to repeat the words elsewhere and his insistence on suppressing feelings suggest a controlled and potentially strategic avowal rather than a reflex-like outburst. Whether his professed love is sincere is narratively questionable but orthogonal to its assertoric force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Jag älskar er — utan tvivel — kan ni tveka på det?” (“I love you—without a doubt—can you doubt it?”)\",\"supports\":\"The explicit avowal and challenge to doubt strongly support truth-conditional force.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Miss Julie first asks: “Säg att du älskar mig! Kom och omfamna mig!” Jean responds while “tvekande” (“hesitating”).\",\"supports\":\"The declaration is a prompted response intended to reassure her, not positively presented as an involuntary expressive discharge.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Jean later says, “Jag skall säga det, tusen gånger — sedan — bara icke här! Och framför allt, inga känslor ... Vi måste ta saken kallt!”\",\"supports\":\"His willingness to repeat the formula later, coupled with deliberate emotional restraint, supports controlled avowal and weighs against expressive/reflexive force.\",\"confidence\":0.97},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Jean refuses the intimate pronoun “du,” saying that barriers remain while they are in the house because of the past and the Count.\",\"supports\":\"The retained social distance weakens any reading of the core sentence as enacting a new mutual commitment, while providing contextual tension around the avowal.\",\"confidence\":0.97}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the core utterance as an avowal presented as true. Its hesitation, possible calculation, and class-bound relational tension are adequately treated as context; neither P, E, nor O is required.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
      ],
